<div id="game-wrapper">
  <div class="score-row">
    {{ statCard("Score", "score-display", "0") }} {{ statCard("Level", "level-display", "1") }} {{ statCard("Best",
    "best-display", "0") }}
  </div>

  <div class="difficulty-row">
    <button class="diff-btn active" id="btn-easy" onclick="setDifficulty('easy')">🎵 Easy</button>
    <button class="diff-btn" id="btn-medium" onclick="setDifficulty('medium')">🎶 Medium</button>
    <button class="diff-btn" id="btn-hard" onclick="setDifficulty('hard')">🎸 Hard</button>
  </div>
  <div id="now-playing">🎹 <strong id="song-name">Twinkle Twinkle</strong></div>

  <div class="canvas-wrapper">
    <canvas id="canvas"></canvas>
    <div id="overlay">
      <span class="demo-label" id="demo-label">Live Demo</span>
      <span>🎹</span>
      <h2>Piano Tiles</h2>
      <div id="song-card">
        <div id="card-song">Twinkle Twinkle Little Star</div>
        <div id="card-artist">Traditional · ~1806</div>
        <div id="card-fact">Based on a French melody that Mozart also arranged as famous piano variations.</div>
      </div>
      <p>Tap each tile in time with the music!</p>
      <button class="play-btn" onclick="startGame()">Play Game</button>
    </div>
    <div id="gameover-overlay">
      <span id="go-icon">💀</span>
      <h2 id="go-title">Game Over</h2>
      <div class="summary-row">
        {{ summaryStatCard("Score", "go-score") }} {{ summaryStatCard("Best", "go-best") }} {{ summaryStatCard("Level",
        "go-level", "1") }}
      </div>
      <button class="play-btn" onclick="startGame()">New Game</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="info-section">
    {% call infoDetails("How to Play") %}
    <div class="info-body">
      <h4>Goal</h4>
      <p>Tap colored tiles as they fall in time with the music. Don't miss one or tap empty space!</p>
      <h4>Controls</h4>
      <p>Click or tap on the colored tiles as they scroll down the screen.</p>
      <h4>Difficulty &amp; Songs</h4>
      <p>
        Easy songs (e.g. Twinkle Twinkle) fall slowly. Medium songs fall at a moderate pace. Hard songs (e.g. Für Elise)
        fall fast. Each difficulty picks a random song from its pool.
      </p>
      <h4>Scoring &amp; Levels</h4>
      <p>Each tapped tile scores 10 points. Speed increases every 10 tiles. Level increases every 10 taps.</p>
      <h4>Column Colors &amp; Notes</h4>
      <p>
        Lower-pitched notes appear in left columns (blue, green) and higher-pitched notes in right columns (yellow,
        red). The color helps you identify which note is playing.
      </p>
      <h4>Game Over Conditions</h4>
      <p>You lose if: an untapped tile passes the bottom of the screen, or you click empty space.</p>
    </div>
    {% endcall %} {% call infoDetails("FAQ") %}
    <div class="info-body">
      <h4>What counts as a miss?</h4>
      <p>Any untapped tile that fully passes the bottom of the screen ends the game.</p>
      <h4>What if I tap empty space?</h4>
      <p>Game over immediately — only tap the colored tiles!</p>
      <h4>Why are tiles different colors?</h4>
      <p>
        Each column has its own color: blue (col 1), green (col 2), yellow (col 3), red (col 4). Lower notes are on the
        left, higher notes on the right.
      </p>
      <h4>Is there an end?</h4>
      <p>No — play until you miss or tap empty space. The tiles keep speeding up with each level.</p>
      <h4>Is my best score saved?</h4>
      <p>Yes — your best score is stored in your browser's local storage and persists between sessions.</p>
    </div>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>
</div>

